            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0332" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.1611/188a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Salvadoran Chargé</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Leiva</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-13">May 13, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I was shocked to
                    learn of the injuries which you suffered last night and I hasten to extend to
                    you an expression of my regret. I assure you that the police will make every
                    effort to apprehend the offenders.</p>
                <p>I trust that you will recover promptly and I want you to know that you have my
                    deepest sympathy.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
